{"step_index":134,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:11:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-20T11:41:58+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-20T11:41:59+05:30\nShowing lines 1-50 of 190\n1: # 🚀 NexusMobility — C++ Backend REST API Server\n2: \n3: Modern, thread-safe C++17/20 REST API backend server for the **NexusMobility Smart City Eco-Logistics Platform**. It handles all pathfinding algorithms (Dijkstra with Min-Heap), custom data structures (circular buffers, FIFO queues, LIFO rollback stack), driver partner onboarding, route matching, and real-time sustainability calculations.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 🛠️ Architecture & Tech Stack\n8: - **Standard**: C++17 / C++20\n9: - **Framework**: `cpp-httplib` (High performance multi-threaded HTTP server)\n10: - **Serialization**: `nlohmann/json`\n11: - **Build System**: CMake (≥ 3.16)\n12: - **Port**: `8080` (Default, customizable via CLI argument)\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 📂 Project Structure\n17: \n18: ```text\n19: cpp-backend/\n20: ├── CMakeLists.txt          # Modern CMake build configuration\n21: ├── README.md               # Architecture and execution manual\n22: ├── build.bat               # Windows 1-click build script\n23: ├── run.bat                 # Windows 1-click run script\n24: ├── test_api.ps1            # Comprehensive API test script in PowerShell\n25: ├── test_api.sh             # Bash curl test script\n26: ├── include/\n27: │   ├── Models.hpp          # Structs & JSON serializers (Station, Driver, Trip, etc.)\n28: │   └── NexusEngine.hpp     # Thread-safe core engine interface\n29: └── src/\n30:     ├── NexusEngine.cpp     # Pathfinding, circular buffer, FIFO queue & audit logic\n31:     └── main.cpp            # HTTP server endpoints & CORS headers\n32: ```\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## ⚙️ Building and Running\n37: \n38: ### Prerequisites\n39: - Modern C++ Compiler: GCC 9+, Clang 10+, or Visual Studio 2019+ (MSVC)\n40: - CMake 3.16+\n41: \n42: ### Option 1: Using CMake (Cross-Platform)\n43: \n44: ```bash\n45: cd cpp-backend\n46: mkdir build && cd build\n47: cmake ..\n48: cmake --build . --config Release\n49: ```\n50: "}
{"step_index":135,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:11:59Z","input_tokens":13877,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1451,"content":"The modern, thread-safe **C++ REST API Backend Server** for the **NexusMobility Smart City Eco-Logistics Platform** is complete and fully structured in:\n\n📂 [`cpp-backend/`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend)\n\n---\n\n### 🏗️ Summary of Implemented C++ Backend Architecture\n\n1. **Clean Data Models & Serialization ([`Models.hpp`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/include/Models.hpp))**:\n   - `Station`, `Corridor`, `Passenger`, `Driver`, `Trip`, `AuditAction`, `RouteResult`, and `EcoLeader` with bidirectional `nlohmann::json` serialization macros (`to_json` / `from_json`).\n\n2. **Core Data Structures & Algorithms ([`NexusEngine.hpp`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/include/NexusEngine.hpp) & [`NexusEngine.cpp`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/src/NexusEngine.cpp))**:\n   - **Min-Heap Dijkstra Algorithm**: Computes shortest travel corridor paths, mileage, transit minutes, tiered pooled fares, and CO₂ savings metrics using `std::priority_queue`.\n   - **5-Slot Priority Standby Ring Buffer**: Fixed capacity array (`std::array<Passenger, 5>`) with modulo arithmetic (`(head + 1) % 5`), overflow detection, and auto-dispatch capability.\n   - **Commuter Dispatch FIFO Pipeline**: Thread-safe queue (`std::deque<Passenger>`) for live passenger onboarding and dispatch.\n   - **Driver Fleet & Vehicle Onboarding**: 4-seat modular capacity management, route overlap matching badging, and $O(1)$ fast lookup for Driver IDs and Booking Refs.\n   - **LIFO Audit Rollback Stack**: Stack-based transaction reversal (`revertLatestConfirmation()`) to safely roll back dispatched trips, restore vehicle seats, and restore passenger statuses.\n   - **One-Click Rush-Hour Simulation**: Instant state seeder for demos.\n\n3. **Multi-Threaded REST API Server ([`main.cpp`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/src/main.cpp))**:\n   - Built on `cpp-httplib` with complete CORS support (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`).\n   - Serves 22 production REST endpoints under `/api/` (routes, passengers, priority-lounge, drivers, fleet, trips, audit/rollback, analytics, and demo loader).\n\n4. **Build, Test, and Run Tooling**:\n   - **CMake Build**: [`CMakeLists.txt`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/CMakeLists.txt) with automated `FetchContent` for `cpp-httplib` and `nlohmann/json`.\n   - **Windows Scripts**: [`build.bat`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/build.bat) & [`run.bat`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/run.bat).\n   - **Test Suites**: [`test_api.ps1`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/test_api.ps1) (PowerShell) and [`test_api.sh`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/test_api.sh) (Bash curl).\n   - **Documentation**: [`README.md`](file:///C:/Users/Kartik%20Bhosle/.gemini/antigravity/brain/6976d1a8-fd03-4453-a790-acd552e1861a/cpp-backend/README.md).\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Quick Start Instructions\n\n#### On Windows:\n```cmd\ncd cpp-backend\nbuild.bat\nrun.bat\n```\n\n#### On Linux / macOS:\n```bash\ncd cpp-backend\nmkdir build && cd build\ncmake ..\ncmake --build . --config Release\n./nexus_backend\n```\n\n#### Running Automated API Tests:\n```powershell\n# PowerShell\n.\\test_api.ps1\n```\n```bash\n# Bash\nchmod +x test_api.sh && ./test_api.sh\n```\n\nLet me know if you would like me to link `app.js` with dynamic REST queries to the C++ server or add any additional transit simulation endpoints!"}
